{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2842 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "124de0cd280459fb705e9ccbe4ef7ab95ecae41bfd8bcad9a40c28abe94ad1a0" :edb/db-before-t 2841 :edb/db-after-t 2842 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536154 50 #inst "2026-10-09T17:19:09.948Z" 13194139536154 true] [17592186229578 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} - 12y = 12x - 13$.\n\nFind the particular solution $y_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n$y_{p}(x) =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536154 false] [17592186229578 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-12y=12x-13.\n$$\n\nFind the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536154 true] [17592186229578 1145 "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\alpha -12(\\alpha x+\\beta )=12x-13\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-12\\alpha x+(\\alpha -12\\beta )=12x-13.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-12\\alpha =12\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\alpha -12\\beta =-13\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,\\,\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-x+1.\n$$" 13194139536154 true] [17592186229578 1145 "Try $y_p=ax+b$, so $y_p^{\\prime}=a$. Substitution gives $a-12(ax+b)=12x-13$. Comparing coefficients, $-12a=12$ and $a-12b=-13$. Thus $a=-1$, $b=1$, and $y_p(x)=1-x$." 13194139536154 false]] :edb/tempids {}}
